DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Pretend City Children's Museum - Events\\nAges: 0-6
 0 months\\nCategory: Play & Games\\n\\nGet messy. Create together.\nOur im
 mersive summer art exhibit invites families to paint\, sculpt\, build\, an
 d explore without limits. This summer\, art isn&#8217\;t something you loo
 k at—it&#8217\;s something to experience together. Every visit brings so
 mething new\, where creativity grows through art\, movement\, and play.\n9
  am &#8211\; 3:00 pm\nThis exhibit is included in museum admission. Space
  is limited! Book your tickets now. \nArtists in Action\n\nJune\nSunday
 \, June 7th &#8211\; Artsy 101 | Time: 11 AM &#8211\; 12 PM\nTuesday\, Jun
 e 9th &#8211\; In-house Artist | Time: 11 AM &#8211\; 12 PM\nThursday\, Ju
 ne 25th &#8211\; In-house Artist | Time: 11 AM &#8211\; 12 PM\nSaturday\, 
 June 27th &#8211\; Chuck Jones Center for Creativity | Time: 11 AM &#8211\
 ; 2 PM\nJuly\nSunday\, July 5th &#8211\; Sawdust Art Festival’s Art Educ
 ation Department | Time: 11 AM &#8211\; 12 PM\nTuesday\, July 21st &#8211\
 ; In-house Artist | Time: 11 AM &#8211\; 12 PM\nSaturday\, July 25th &#821
 1\; Chuck Jones Center for Creativity | Time: 11 AM &#8211\; 2 PM\nTuesday
 \, July 28th &#8211\; In-house Artist | Time: 11 AM &#8211\; 12 PM\nAugust
 \nSunday\, August 2nd &#8211\; In-house Artist | Time: 11 AM &#8211\; 12 P
 M\nSunday\, August 9th &#8211\; Martin Bruinsma | Time: 11 AM &#8211\; 12 
 PM\nTuesday\, August 18th &#8211\; In-house Artist | Time: 11 AM &#8211\; 
 12 PM\nSaturday\, August 22nd &#8211\; Chuck Jones Center for Creativity |
  Time: 11 AM &#8211\; 2 PM\nTuesday\, August 25th &#8211\; In-house Artist
  | Time: 11 AM &#8211\; 12 PM\n\n\n*Events and dates are subject to change
 .\nPretend City Summer Hours\nOpen Tuesday &#8211\; Sunday\n&#8211\;Closed
  on Mondays except Memorial Day and Labor Day\n&#8211\;Closed on Father&#8
 217\;s Day and Fourth of July\n\nFrequently Asked Questions\nIs the summer
  exhibit included with admission?Yes. The exhibit is included with regular
  museum admission.\nWill there be special programming?Yes. Additional prog
 ramming and special activities will be announced soon.\nWhat ages is this 
 exhibit best for?The exhibit is designed for children ages 2–9 and their
  families.\nDo children need art experience to participate?No. This is an 
 open-ended\, play-based experience where children can explore creativity a
 t their own pace.\nWill it be messy?Yes. This exhibit encourages hands-on 
 creativity\, so we recommend dressing children in clothes that can get mes
 sy.\nAre you open on Mondays?No. Pretend City is closed on Mondays\, excep
 t for Memorial Day and Labor Day.\nWhy does the exhibit close early?The ex
 hibit closes at 3:00 pm to allow time for cleaning and resetting the space
 . The museum remains open until 4:00 pm.\\n\\nMore info: https://www.prete
 ndcity.org/events/wonderstudio/
LOCATION:Pretend City Children's Museum - Events\, 29 Hubble\, Irvine\, CA
 \, 92618
URL:https://www.pretendcity.org/events/wonderstudio/
