DESCRIPTION:Organizer: OCPL - Aliso Viejo Branch\\nCost: free\\nAges: 0-60
  months\\nCategory: Storytime\\n\\nJoin us at the Aliso Viejo Library for 
 a cooking demonstration with Jeffrey Eisner! Limited complimentary books a
 vailable\, while supplies last. No registration required\, all ages welcom
 e. Early arrival suggested.\n\nJeffrey Eisner is a multiple-time #1 bestse
 lling author where his debut cookbook was one of the most sold during the 
 2020 pandemic - a time when people were cooking at home more than ever. Hi
 s trusted and signature recipes earned him numerous repeat appearances on 
 television shows such as Rachael Ray\, Good Morning America\, and The Food
  Network. He develops and tests his recipes based on his travels with some
  of his native New York flair tossed into the mix. When not cooking\, he e
 njoys spoiling his dog\, Banjo the Norwich Terrier. He also loves theatre 
 and pinball. Check him out at pressureluckcooking.com and on the various s
 ocial media platforms.\n\nFor more information\, call 949-360-1730 or emai
 l ocpl.alisoviejo@occr.ocgov.com\n\nThis project is funded in part through
  a grant from the California Department of Aging and administered locally 
 by the Orange County Office on Aging.\\n\\nMore info: https://ocpl.libcal.
 com/event/16818928
LOCATION:Aliso Viejo\, Aliso Viejo
URL:https://ocpl.libcal.com/event/16818928
